<!-- HERO -->
<div class="page-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Sizing Guide</p>
  <h1>Find Your <em>Perfect Fit</em></h1>
  <p>Ensuring the right fit is everything. Use our guide to measure at home or visit us in store for a complimentary sizing.</p>
</div>

<div class="page-wrap">

  <!-- METHODS -->
  <div class="methods-grid">
    <div class="method-card">
      <div class="method-num">01</div>
      <h2 class="method-title">Measure an <em>Existing Ring</em></h2>
      <div class="method-steps">
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">1</div>
          <p>Select a ring that already fits the finger you'd like to wear your new piece on.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">2</div>
          <p>Place the ring on a ruler and measure the internal diameter in millimetres (the distance across the inside of the ring).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">3</div>
          <p>Match your measurement to the chart below. If you fall between two sizes, we recommend choosing the larger size.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="method-tip">
        <strong>Tip:</strong> The best time to measure your finger is at the end of the day when fingers are at their largest. Cold temperatures can cause fingers to shrink.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="method-card" style="background: var(--blush);">
      <div class="method-num">02</div>
      <h2 class="method-title">Measure Your <em>Finger</em></h2>
      <div class="method-steps">
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">1</div>
          <p>Cut a thin strip of paper or use a flexible measuring tape.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">2</div>
          <p>Wrap it snugly around the base of the finger where you want the ring to sit — it should be snug but comfortable enough to slide over your knuckle.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-step">
          <div class="method-step-num">3</div>
          <p>Mark where the paper meets, then measure that length in millimetres — this is your finger circumference. Enter it into our calculator below.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="method-tip">
        <strong>Tip:</strong> Measure 3–4 times and take the average for the most accurate result. Wider band rings may require a half size larger.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- CALCULATOR -->
  <div class="calculator-section">
    <div class="calc-text">
      <p class="eyebrow">Size Calculator</p>
      <h2>Find Your Size <em>Instantly</em></h2>
      <p>Enter your finger circumference or ring diameter and we'll tell you your Melia Nae size. Measurements in millimetres or inches.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="calc-widget">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:16px;margin-bottom:20px;">
        <div style="flex:1;">
          <p class="calc-label" style="margin-bottom:8px;">Measurement Type</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;">
            <button class="unit-btn active" id="typeCirc" onclick="setType('circ')">Circumference</button>
            <button class="unit-btn" id="typeDiam" onclick="setType('diam')">Diameter</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="calc-label" style="margin-bottom:8px;">Unit</p>
          <div class="calc-unit-toggle">
            <button class="unit-btn active" id="unitMm" onclick="setUnit('mm')">mm</button>
            <button class="unit-btn" id="unitIn" onclick="setUnit('in')">in</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="calc-label" id="inputLabel">Enter circumference (mm)</p>
      <div class="calc-input-row">
        <input type="number" class="calc-input" id="measureInput" placeholder="e.g. 52.5" oninput="calculateSize()" step="0.1" min="0" />
      </div>
      <div class="calc-result" id="calcResult">
        <p class="result-placeholder">Enter your measurement above</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

